  "generated_text": "1. **Identify the equations:**\n   \\[\n   x + y = 2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   xy - z^2 = 1\n   \\]\n\n2. **Substitute $x + y = 2$ into $xy - z^2 = 1$:**\n   \\[\n   xy = 1 + z^2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (x + y)^2 = 4\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x^2 + 2xy + y^2 = 4\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x^2 + 2(1 + z^2) + y^2 = 4\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x^2 + y^2 + 2z^2 = 2\n   \\]\n\n3. **Solve for $x^2 + y^2$:**\n   \\[\n   x^2 + y^2 = 2 - 2z^2\n   \\]\n\n4. **Analyze the inequality:**\n   Since $x^2 + y^2 \\geq 0$, we have:\n   \\[\n   2 - 2z^2 \\geq 0",
